1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,580
In the last video,

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:05,490
I introduced the concept of
continuous improvements.

3
00:00:05,490 --> 00:00:07,920
We explored in depth
how working in

4
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:11,430
a controlled environment
can optimize your outcomes.

5
00:00:11,430 --> 00:00:13,800
In this video, we're
going to keep on

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,480
that same path of uncovering

7
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:17,745
methods for continuous
improvements.

8
00:00:17,745 --> 00:00:20,955
We'll start with data-driven
improvement frameworks.

9
00:00:20,955 --> 00:00:23,850
Data-driven improvement
frameworks are techniques

10
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:27,045
used to make decisions
based on actual data.

11
00:00:27,045 --> 00:00:30,510
The first data-driven improvement
framework we'll cover

12
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:32,250
may be familiar to you since

13
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:34,230
we discussed it in
a previous course.

14
00:00:34,230 --> 00:00:41,499
Recall that D-M-A-I-C, or DMAIC,
stands for define, measure,

15
00:00:41,499 --> 00:00:45,530
analyze, improve, and
control, and it maps

16
00:00:45,530 --> 00:00:47,330
out five steps that you can

17
00:00:47,330 --> 00:00:50,110
take when working toward
continuous improvements.

18
00:00:50,110 --> 00:00:51,770
When considering how you

19
00:00:51,770 --> 00:00:53,630
can improve customer experiences,

20
00:00:53,630 --> 00:00:55,025
start with the following:

21
00:00:55,025 --> 00:00:57,770
First, you'll need to define
the business problem, goals,

22
00:00:57,770 --> 00:01:01,145
resources, project scope,
and project timeline.

23
00:01:01,145 --> 00:01:03,200
Next, measure.

24
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,380
Here, you'll conduct
performance metrics and data

25
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:10,175
collection to establish
baselines and measure success.

26
00:01:10,175 --> 00:01:12,830
Then, analyze. Work to find

27
00:01:12,830 --> 00:01:16,060
the root causes of problems
and understand their impact.

28
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:17,925
Next, improve.

29
00:01:17,925 --> 00:01:19,414
This means implementing

30
00:01:19,414 --> 00:01:21,805
a reasonable solution
to the problem.

31
00:01:21,805 --> 00:01:23,695
Lastly, control.

32
00:01:23,695 --> 00:01:25,070
This is where you'll implement

33
00:01:25,070 --> 00:01:26,720
the changes and stay on top of

34
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:30,955
monitoring the updated
processes you've established.

35
00:01:30,955 --> 00:01:34,550
Another framework you can
refer to when working through

36
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:38,200
continuous improvements is PDCA.

37
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:41,150
PDCA is a four-step process

38
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:43,925
that focuses on
identifying a problem,

39
00:01:43,925 --> 00:01:46,850
fixing that issue, assessing
whether the fix was

40
00:01:46,850 --> 00:01:50,075
successful, and fine-tuning
the final fix.

41
00:01:50,075 --> 00:01:54,510
The steps are as
follows: First, plan.

42
00:01:54,510 --> 00:01:56,750
Here, you'll identify
the issue and

43
00:01:56,750 --> 00:02:00,290
root cause and brainstorm
solutions to the problem.

44
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:03,200
Let's say that one type of
plant isn't selling well,

45
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,640
which means the warehouse is

46
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:07,219
full of a particular species.

47
00:02:07,219 --> 00:02:09,755
If you don't do something fast,

48
00:02:09,755 --> 00:02:11,850
the plants may die soon.

49
00:02:11,850 --> 00:02:14,540
What are some viable solutions?

50
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:17,360
You propose moving the
items from the bottom

51
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:19,985
of the sales page on
the website to the top so

52
00:02:19,985 --> 00:02:22,085
those plants are
front and center.

53
00:02:22,085 --> 00:02:24,950
You could also send out
email marketing campaigns

54
00:02:24,950 --> 00:02:28,475
featuring that plant, where you
offer customers a buy one,

55
00:02:28,475 --> 00:02:30,785
get one offer on the plant.

56
00:02:30,785 --> 00:02:34,135
Second, do, or fix the problem.

57
00:02:34,135 --> 00:02:36,920
In this case, your sponsor
decided that they didn't

58
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,270
feel comfortable giving plants

59
00:02:38,270 --> 00:02:39,770
away if they could still profit.

60
00:02:39,770 --> 00:02:42,440
You've decided to go
with the first option:

61
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:46,145
moving the plant to a more
prominent part of the website.

62
00:02:46,145 --> 00:02:49,085
Your hypothesis is that
the best way to shift

63
00:02:49,085 --> 00:02:50,750
older inventory is to put it in

64
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:52,990
a place that
customers can't miss.

65
00:02:52,990 --> 00:02:55,505
The next part of this
framework is check.

66
00:02:55,505 --> 00:02:57,230
Compare your results to the goal

67
00:02:57,230 --> 00:02:59,375
to find out if the
problem is fixed.

68
00:02:59,375 --> 00:03:01,850
Now you wait one
week and notice if

69
00:03:01,850 --> 00:03:04,775
the sales numbers go up for
that plant. If they did,

70
00:03:04,775 --> 00:03:07,340
your hypothesis is
correct and you've saved

71
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:08,630
some plant lives and helped

72
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:10,460
Office Green avoid
financial loss.

73
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:13,415
Nice job! Finally, act,

74
00:03:13,415 --> 00:03:16,840
or fine-tune the fix to ensure
continuous improvement.

75
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:20,435
In our example, you decide
to reorganize the website.

76
00:03:20,435 --> 00:03:22,835
In the future, all
overstocked plants

77
00:03:22,835 --> 00:03:25,405
will get a prominent
place on the website.

78
00:03:25,405 --> 00:03:28,960
Both PDCA and DMAIC are

79
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:31,360
great problem-solving
frameworks to apply in

80
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:34,269
your day-to-day life
and in the workplace.

81
00:03:34,269 --> 00:03:37,390
These frameworks help
you to identify issues,

82
00:03:37,390 --> 00:03:40,690
reduce errors, and
optimize your processes.

83
00:03:40,690 --> 00:03:42,610
I encourage you to think about

84
00:03:42,610 --> 00:03:44,500
these techniques next
time you encounter

85
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:46,240
a problem or notice room for

86
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:48,370
improvement within a workflow.

87
00:03:48,370 --> 00:03:50,320
You'll be surprised at how

88
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:54,215
a simple framework can help
set you up for success.

89
00:03:54,215 --> 00:03:56,695
Awesome! Now you know more about

90
00:03:56,695 --> 00:03:59,695
advocating for and creating
continuous improvements.

91
00:03:59,695 --> 00:04:02,680
We also defined and went
through some examples of using

92
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:07,640
frameworks DMAIC and PDCA
for process improvements.

93
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,650
Now that you know the basics of

94
00:04:09,650 --> 00:04:12,065
continuous improvement
and process improvement,

95
00:04:12,065 --> 00:04:13,790
we'll discuss the
differences between

96
00:04:13,790 --> 00:04:16,595
projects and programs
and how they intersect.

97
00:04:16,595 --> 00:04:19,080
I'll meet you in the next video.
